💧 Smart Water Tank Monitoring System using IoT

> An IoT-based system that monitors water levels in real time and sends automatic **SMS/buzzer alerts** for low water, full tank, and overflow conditions — helping prevent water wastage and manual monitoring hassle.

---

## 📌 Short Description 

An IoT-powered smart water tank monitoring system that uses an ultrasonic sensor to track real-time water levels and triggers SMS and buzzer alerts for low/high water conditions — eliminating the need for manual checks and reducing water wastage.

---

## 📖 Overview

Manually checking water tank levels is inefficient and often leads to overflow or dry-run situations that waste water and damage motors. This project automates the process using an **ultrasonic distance sensor** to continuously measure water level, a **microcontroller** to process the readings, and a **GSM module + buzzer** to alert the user instantly via SMS and sound when the level crosses defined thresholds — with no app or internet dependency required.

---

## ✨ Features

- 📏 Real-time water level measurement using ultrasonic sensing
- 🔔 Instant buzzer alert for critical levels (low/overflow)
- 📩 Automatic SMS notification to the owner's phone via GSM module
- ⚙️ Configurable threshold levels (low, medium, full)
- 🔋 Low-cost, low-power, and easy to deploy on any tank
- 🚫 No internet/Wi-Fi dependency — works purely over GSM network

---

## 🛠️ Hardware Components

| Component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Microcontroller (Arduino/NodeMCU/ESP32) | Core processing unit |
| Ultrasonic Sensor (HC-SR04) | Measures water level/distance |
| GSM Module (SIM800L/SIM900) | Sends SMS alerts |
| Buzzer | Local audible alert |
| Relay Module (optional) | Auto motor ON/OFF control |
| Power Supply (5V/12V adapter) | Powers the circuit |
| Jumper Wires & Breadboard/PCB | Circuit connections |

---

## ⚙️ Working Principle

1. The **ultrasonic sensor** is mounted at the top of the tank and continuously measures the distance to the water surface.
2. The **microcontroller** converts this distance into a water level percentage.
3. Based on predefined thresholds:
   - **Low level** → Buzzer + SMS alert: "Water level low, please refill."
   - **Full/Overflow level** → Buzzer + SMS alert: "Tank full, stop the motor."
4. (Optional) A **relay module** can automatically switch the motor pump ON/OFF based on the level, removing manual intervention entirely.

